WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.360
If you remove one receptor from a mouse, which neurons disappear, and when?

2
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:13.150
A knockout mouse is one in which a chosen gene has been disrupted.

3
00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:17.923
It makes no working protein, or no working form of one protein.

4
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:22.187
Delete each neurotrophin or Trk gene, one at a time.

5
00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:25.107
The family sorts by which neurons are lost.

6
00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:29.487
Start with TrkA, and the sympathetic ganglion in the neck.

7
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.890
Anne Fagan and colleagues counted its cells at several ages.

8
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.430
At embryonic day 13.5, the count was normal.

9
00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:44.413
If TrkA is needed for survival, not for making the neurons, what should happen next?

10
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:52.587
The mutant fell steadily behind.

11
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.330
At birth it had about half as many neurons as control ganglia.

12
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.510
By postnatal day 9, nearly all of its principal neurons were gone.

13
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.860
Over those embryonic ages, dividing cells were no fewer than in controls.

14
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.040
Dying cells, with shrunken nuclei, increased.

15
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.360
So the neurons were made, and then they died.

16
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.670
Now the other pairs.

17
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:21.050
Mice lacking NGF or TrkA lose sympathetic neurons.

18
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:26.073
They also lose many small sensory neurons that sense pain and heat.

19
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:32.527
Mice lacking BDNF lose vestibular neurons, which sense balance and head movement.

20
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.160
They also lose many nodose-petrosal neurons, which carry signals from the heart,

21
00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.540
lungs and gut.

22
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.240
Mice lacking NT-4 lose nodose-petrosal neurons too.

23
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:51.040
And mice lacking NT-3 or TrkC lose the sensory neurons that report where a limb is.

24
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.860
These mice move and hold their limbs abnormally.

25
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:58.113
In this grid, lose means fewer neurons.

26
00:01:59.153 --> 00:02:03.473
Usually part of a ganglion survives, but some groups are lost almost entirely.

27
00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:06.633
Each pair has its own pattern of loss.

28
00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:09.313
But the map has overlaps.

29
00:02:10.173 --> 00:02:14.533
NT-3 prefers TrkC, yet it also activates TrkA and TrkB.

30
00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:20.867
Should a mouse lacking NT-3 lose more neurons, or fewer, than one lacking TrkC?

31
00:02:27.217 --> 00:02:33.657
Expect more. In many ganglia at the same age, mice lacking NT-3 lose more neurons

32
00:02:33.657 --> 00:02:35.077
than mice lacking TrkC.

33
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:40.110
That fits NT-3 also acting through TrkA and TrkB.

34
00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.630
The size of the gap depends on the ganglion and age.

35
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.660
Some populations also need more than one factor, at different stages.

36
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.040
The takeaway: each factor and receptor pair has its own pattern of loss.

37
00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.080
In the sympathetic ganglion, neurons were made, then lost.
